 "unresolved": [],
 "observations": [
  "The page number «252» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it. The page has no signature. Two columns divided by a vertical rule, as on pp. [249]-251 (JP2 0283-0285), transcribed column by column: the left column L01-L48, the right L49-L97; the letter heads «I.» (L14), «J.» (L28), «K.» (L38), «L.» (L59) and «M.» (L80) in bold, centred in their columns, each after a blank line; each entry begins at the edge of its column, its further lines indented, the subentries with a dash indented less, and the subentries of a subentry («— — der Sonne», L63) with two dashes.",
  "Roman numerals set with a lowercase l in place of an I, as on pp. 250-251 (JP2 0284-0285): «XVIlI» (L27), «Xl» (L35), «XXIl» (L46), «XIIl» (L86), «XXl» (L87); transcribed as printed. The sort is told apart by its top: the l has a flag on the left only, the I serifs on both sides.",
  "The semicolon of L03 stands after a thin space (9 px); written with a space. L64: the dash of «81—86» is printed with a gap: a fragment of 6 px after the 1, then 8 px of white, then the dash (25 px); written —. The other dashes are long (27-47 px). L05: a speck before the dash; L31: a speck below the j of «Sternjahr»; not transcribed. L82: «al-Ma’mūn», the hamza as an apostrophe ’. L37: «Judices (= Domini)»; L07: «(= Aufgänge», the = with a space after the parenthesis.",
